The reordering of the checks caused the function to issue warnings for guest frame numbers (GFNs) that were not covered by any MTRRs. Specifically, the check for whether the memory type was not contained in any MTRRs was moved after the warning check for partial mappings, leading to excessive warnings when the type remained -1 (indicating no MTRR coverage).

